VALUES ('bd114ed4-a706-5919-bc0e-1a6139f99acb', 'Tax Jurisdiction', 'Maintain Tax Jurisdiction records', 'Create, find and maintain Tax Jurisdiction records. The list shows every Tax Jurisdiction you have access to — select a row to open it, or use New to add one. Each row is a single Tax Jurisdiction, described by 3 fields.

Id is unique: no two Tax Jurisdiction records may share the same value, and a save that would duplicate one is rejected. Status must be filled in before the record can be saved.

Every Tax Jurisdiction points at Organization. Choose the linked record from the lookup on those fields rather than typing an identifier.

Every save starts as a Draft. The business rules and workflows attached to Tax Jurisdiction then run together in a single transaction: if all of them succeed the record becomes Final; if any of them fails, nothing they changed is kept — the record stays Draft and the reason is written onto it so you can fix the cause and retry. A Tax Jurisdiction with no rules or workflows attached is marked Final immediately.', 'percent', 'M', FALSE, TRUE, 'U', TRUE, 'system', 'system', NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
